  "title": "Ramsey properties of Cayley graphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture There exists a fixed constant $c$ so that every abelian group $G$ has a subset $S \\subseteq G$ with $-S = S$ so that the Cayley graph ${\\mathit Cayley}(G,S)$ has no clique or independent set of size $> c \\log |G|$.",
